Working with Graphics
Work with Graphics
Plant Simulation displays objects with graphics, which are structured in one or several graphic groups.
Graphic groups of objects and Frames consist of one or more graphics and have a name that is unique
for this object. This is similar to the 2D icons of the simulation objects. You can define a graphic group to
either be external or internal.
External graphic groups represent the object toward the outside, while internal graphic groups are
used to decorate the inside of the object. The properties which graphic groups are internal or locked
are, together with the graphic structure, an object property that can be inherited. A graphic group can
be permanently shown or hidden to allow switching between alternative visual representations. Each
simulation object or animatable object contains at least one external graphic group named default
and optionally any number of alternative or additional graphic groups, which you can show or hide
independent of each other.
In addition, a Frame initially contains one internal graphic group named deco. The visibility of the graphic
groups is an object property which can be inherited independent from the graphic structure and the
properties internal and locked. You can create, delete, or configure graphic groups on the tab Graphics
[tab] in the dialog Edit 3D Properties and in the dialog Show Graphic Structure [button].
Icon looks like this means that the graphic group is
visible
visible
