Duplicate Graphics
You can duplicate the graphic you selected in the 3D window.
To duplicate the selected graphic, hold down Ctrl+Shift and click the left mouse button in the 3D window
at a different position.
Plant Simulation does not create a copy of the graphic, but the new graphic references the duplicated
graphic. This considerably reduces memory consumption.
Plant Simulation shows that the graphic is referenced with a diamond 
  in the dialog Show Graphic
Structure.
Edit Grouped Graphics
You can edit grouped graphics, i.e., the graphic group as a whole.
To move, rotate, or scale several graphics at the same time while retaining their positions to each other,
you can group them and manipulate the group as a whole.
Note
If you change any graphic or the graphic structure of a class object, this also changes all inherited
objects. If you change the graphics of a derived object, this only changes the object in which you
make the changes because Plant Simulation turns off graphic inheritance if it has not been deactivated
already. As deactivating graphic inheritance causes graphics to be duplicated, we strongly advise you to
make changes in the class object as far as possible.
Duplicate Graphics
10-990 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

To group several graphics:
• Hold down Shift and click the objects to select them or drag a marquee over them.
• Click 
  Group Graphics on the Edit ribbon tab or press Ctrl+G. Plant Simulation creates a single new
group.
• Then, move, rotate, scale, or zoom the group as you do a single graphic.
• Naturally you can also move, rotate, scale, or zoom the group on the Tab Transformation in the dialog
Edit 3D Properties.
To restore the previous structure of the graphics:
• Select the newly created group.
• Click 
  Ungroup Group of Graphics on the Edit ribbon tab or press Ctrl+U to replace this group with
the contained graphics again.
