Model Your Own 3D Graphic
You can model your own 3D graphic for a simulation object, by inserting one or several of these Shapes.
Barred Area, Box, Cone, Cuboid, Cylinder, Dimensioning, Factory Walls, Fence, Mezzanine, Rack,
Sphere, Stairs, Text, or Textured Plate.
• Click the shape you want to create. In our example we create a cuboid 
 .
• Select the Graphic Group to which you want to add the cuboid.
• Type in the Dimension X/Width, the Dimension Y/Depth, and the Dimension Z/Height of the cuboid.
• To create the cuboid, click Create. 3D attaches the cuboid to the mouse pointer. Drag the mouse to the
position at which you would like to insert it and click the left mouse button. To cancel inserting, click the
right mouse button or press Esc.
• To change the position, the rotation, or the scale of the shape after you inserted it, select it and click
3D Properties > Tab Transformation on the Home ribbon tab. Then change the settings according to
your needs.
Model Your Own 3D Graphic
Plant Simulation Help 10-999
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• To set if the cuboid is an obstacle for the worker, select it. Then, click Edit 3D Properties on the Home
ribbon tab and click the Tab Graphic Settings.
• To assign a color and a material, select the cuboid and click 3D Properties on the Home ribbon tab.
Then, click the Tab Material.
Model Your Own 3D Graphic
10-1000 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• To create a more complex graphic, insert several shapes and position, rotate, scale or color them.
In addition to the pre-defined shapes you can copy graphics from other graphic groups or import
graphics from graphic files.
• To delete the shape, click it with the right mouse button and click 
  on the mini toolbar or select Show
Graphic Structure.
If the graphic group to which you added the shape, deco in our case, is not expanded already, expand it.
Click the node of the shape you want to delete with the right mouse button. Select Delete.
