Set How Plant Simulation Shows an Object
Depending on which level of the object hierarchy you open a window, an object can look different.
For this reason we differentiate between the outside representation of the object and the inside
representation of the object:
• The outside representation of a Frame designates the entirety of all graphics, which will be selected
when you click the Frame in a window that opened the location of this Frame.
This includes:
Set How Plant Simulation Shows an Object
10-1014 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

◦ Its graphic groups, which are marked as Visible [graphic group] and External [graphic group].
◦ Contained objects, which are not explicitly excluded from the parent outside representation, i. e., for
which you selected Exclude From "Show content" of the Location. This applies only if you selected
Show Content for the Frame.
• The outside representation of other objects includes the following:
◦ Its graphic groups, which are marked as Visible [graphic group].
◦ Its state graphics, which you set according to the Orientation [state graphic].
◦ Its material flow direction if the object is length-oriented.
• The inside representation of a Frame designates the entirety of all graphics, which are shown, when
you open a Frame in a window.
This includes:
◦ Its graphic groups, which are marked as Visible [graphic group] and Internal [graphic group].
◦ The outside representation of its contained objects and Frames.
• The inside representation of other objects includes:.
◦ Its graphic groups, which are marked as Visible [graphic group].
◦ Its state graphics, which you set according to the Orientation [state graphic].
◦ The outside representation of its contained objects.
When editing the object, it might be helpful to show the outside representation and the inside
representation at the same time. To do so, activate Show External Graphic Groups in a window, which
contains the object you are editing.
In the active window, you can, in addition, show or hide the following:
• All Connectors, Interfaces, and Markers by clicking the button Show Connections.
• The material flow direction arrows on all length-oriented objects by clicking the button Show Material
Flow Directions [button].
